                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "633c1b64-2589-387b-a3fc-17735ec8357c",
                        "entry_id": "7d621dd8-37f9-3841-8cf8-aa13070e5dd9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "биохим. фермент, который катализирует гидролиз сахарозы"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e29d4ac2-ee88-4bf5-8484-2f7b8cacade2",
                                "sense_id": "633c1b64-2589-387b-a3fc-17735ec8357c",
                                "text": "В картофеле обнаружены ферменты — диастаза, каталаза, инвертаза, тирозиназа, пероксидаза и лактолаза, дающая спирт и молочную кислоту."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfc7b05e-f62a-427d-976e-6a065c6d8782",
                                "sense_id": "633c1b64-2589-387b-a3fc-17735ec8357c",
                                "text": "Разложение сахарозы в пищеварительной системе животных и человека происходит под воздействием фермента инвертазы, а сам процесс называют инверсией сахара."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db5623eb-3654-4379-9a16-7b5c61aaf349",
                                "sense_id": "633c1b64-2589-387b-a3fc-17735ec8357c",
                                "text": "В состав панкреатического сока входят ферменты, имеющие большое значение в процессах пищеварения, — трипсин, липаза, амилаза, мальтаза, лактаза, инвертаза, нуклеаза, а также в незначительном количестве трепсин и ренин."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4faef7fc-9f15-4ca7-93e4-f6f9edebc7d8",
                        "source_entry_id": "7d621dd8-37f9-3841-8cf8-aa13070e5dd9",
                        "source_sense_id": "633c1b64-2589-387b-a3fc-17735ec8357c",
                        "target_lang_word": "invertase",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "invertase",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "143ce320-ee67-3823-bb25-1ee64ae292b3",
                                        "entry_id": "661ffeb1-d307-3cec-9d16-3b34ddd257e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of sucrose into glucose and fructose (invert sugar), used by bees to produce honey and in the food industry to soften chocolate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6614f97-bc68-4e34-9490-62b0b14a7901",
                                                "sense_id": "143ce320-ee67-3823-bb25-1ee64ae292b3",
                                                "text": "The costs incurred for the processing of sucrose with invertase could be considerably reduced with the introduction of immobilised invertases, by adopting technology similar to that developed for glucose isomerase."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca4c1bf6-9ff1-487e-838a-24abd51d90ab",
                                                "sense_id": "143ce320-ee67-3823-bb25-1ee64ae292b3",
                                                "text": "The disaccharide sucrose and the trisaccharide raffinose are both substrates of invertase. Invertase is encoded by the SUC genes from which six unlinked loci have been identified (SUC1-SUC5, SUC7), which are dipersed through the yeast genome (Lampen, 1968; Ouwehand and van Wijk, 1972; Ottolenghi, 1971)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65942b84-5971-43a2-936d-603b61742dfd",
                                                "sense_id": "143ce320-ee67-3823-bb25-1ee64ae292b3",
                                                "text": "Up-regulation of these invertases is a common response to infection (Hall and Williams, 2000)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de8ced1d-3ca8-4f60-add7-fa5c615b1dc4",
                                                "sense_id": "143ce320-ee67-3823-bb25-1ee64ae292b3",
                                                "text": "2013, Maria Kamiko Kadowaki, Rite de Cássia Garcia Simão, Jose Luís da Conceição Silva, Clarice Aoki Osaku, Luis Henrique Souza Guimarāes, 1: Biotechnical Advances in Fungal Invertases, Maria de Lourdes T. M. Polizeli, Mahendra Rai (editors), Fungal Enzymes, page 14,\nThe methods used for the immobilization of fungal invertases include adsorption, covalent binding, cross-linking and entrapment (Uzun et al. 2011).\nNelson and Griffin (1916) reported that invertase was the first enzyme to be immobilized, and it was bound on charcoal and aluminium hydroxide. Subsequently, mant fungal invertases have been immobilized onto a variety of media […] ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
